      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 5.24,
          "end": 5.72,
          "en": "All right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.72,
          "end": 10.01,
          "en": "In this lecture we are going to talk about bottom up approach with tabulation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 10.01,
          "end": 14.66,
          "en": "So in case of top down approach first we divide the problem into smaller problems.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 14.66,
          "end": 17.42,
          "en": "Then we solve these problems and combine them together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 17.42,
          "end": 20.72,
          "en": "But in case of bottom up approach we do the opposite.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.72,
          "end": 26.24,
          "en": "Which means we start from the smaller problem and slowly inch towards the bigger problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 26.24,
          "end": 31.04,
          "en": "So it is the opposite of the top down approach and this avoids the recursion.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 31.04,
          "end": 33.89,
          "en": "In this approach we solve the problem bottom up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 33.89,
          "end": 39.41,
          "en": "This is typically done by filling up the n dimensional table based on the result in the table.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 39.41,
          "end": 42.68,
          "en": "The solution to the original problem is then computed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 42.68,
          "end": 45.59,
          "en": "So here again the formula remains the same as you remember.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 45.59,
          "end": 47.51,
          "en": "In case of the top down approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 47.51,
          "end": 50,
          "en": "We have filled the this temporary table.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 50,
          "end": 55.22,
          "en": "So in case of top down approach we have started from the top problem which is ef6.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 55.22,
          "end": 57.5,
          "en": "So in this case we want to calculate Ef6.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 57.5,
          "end": 61.82,
          "en": "And we have started this one then calculated the F5 then F3.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 61.82,
          "end": 65.75,
          "en": "And a question comes from F6 to towards to F1.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 65.77,
          "end": 68.68,
          "en": "but in this case we are going to start from the bottom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 68.68,
          "end": 70.36,
          "en": "So in the bottom we have F3.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 70.36,
          "end": 71.74,
          "en": "So we will calculate F3.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 71.74,
          "end": 77.08,
          "en": "Then we are going to calculate F4 which is the sum of the previous two elements f2 and f3 is going to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 77.08,
          "end": 78.03999999999999,
          "en": "be two.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 78.07,
          "end": 79.96000000000001,
          "en": "Then we are going to calculate F5.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.96000000000001,
          "end": 81.52,
          "en": "So in this case f5 is three.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 81.52,
          "end": 83.5,
          "en": "Then we are going to calculate F6.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83.5,
          "end": 86.74,
          "en": "So in this case F6 is going to be is going to be five.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.74,
          "end": 89.68,
          "en": "So that's how the bottom up approach works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.68,
          "end": 92.28999999999999,
          "en": "And as we mentioned it's not using the recursion.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.28999999999999,
          "end": 93.85,
          "en": "It's going to use the iteration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.85,
          "end": 98.59,
          "en": "So in case of bottom up approach the Fibonacci function is going to be like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.59,
          "end": 102.37,
          "en": "So here again it's going to take as a parameter number which is n.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.4,
          "end": 107.68,
          "en": "Then it's going to check that if n is less than zero it means that we cannot calculate the Fibonacci",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 107.71000000000001,
          "end": 108.94,
          "en": "for negative numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.94,
          "end": 114.13,
          "en": "Then the next thing that we do, we know that if n is equal to zero, it's going to return zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 114.13,
          "end": 116.56,
          "en": "If n is equal to one, it's going to return one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.56,
          "end": 120.91,
          "en": "Then we are going to initialize the variables to store the two previous Fibonacci series.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 120.91,
          "end": 123.49,
          "en": "So in this case we are just going to put a first.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.49,
          "end": 125.47,
          "en": "Previous is going to be the previous one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125.47,
          "end": 127.9,
          "en": "And the second previous is going to be the previous two.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 127.93,
          "end": 129.88,
          "en": "So in our case one and zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.88,
          "end": 133.05,
          "en": "And the current number is going to be we are going to start from zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.08,
          "end": 136.07999999999998,
          "en": "Then we are going to start to iterate from two to n.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 136.07999999999998,
          "end": 140.49,
          "en": "So if I is equal to two, we are just going to calculate the current based on the previous one and then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 140.52,
          "end": 141.24,
          "en": "the previous two.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 141.27,
          "end": 145.35,
          "en": "Then we are going to take the previous one and assign it to previous two, and the current one is going",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 145.35,
          "end": 146.55,
          "en": "to be the previous one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.55,
          "end": 148.5,
          "en": "Then we are going to return the current element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 148.5,
          "end": 152.85,
          "en": "So that's how the bottom up approach looks like in case of Fibonacci.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.85,
          "end": 156.81,
          "en": "So here in the code I'm going to show you how both of them are working.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 156.81,
          "end": 159.81,
          "en": "So I've just put the Fibonacci top down over here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 159.81,
          "end": 161.07,
          "en": "So as you can see.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 161.1,
          "end": 163.5,
          "en": "So we are using recursive approach over here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 163.5,
          "end": 166.17000000000002,
          "en": "So what I'm going to do I'll just go ahead and run this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
